<p>Passengers and crew began leaving the Dutch-flagged MV Hondius in Tenerife, Spain, on Sunday after a hantavirus outbreak linked to three deaths, as governments arranged military, charter and special flights to repatriate people by nationality. U.S. health officials said one of 17 American evacuees tested positive for hantavirus but had no symptoms, while another had mild symptoms; both traveled in aircraft biocontainment units, and some Americans were being taken to the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha for assessment. France said one of five French nationals developed symptoms during the flight home and placed the group in strict isolation. French officials later said the passenger tested positive and her condition deteriorated overnight, CBS News reported. Spain’s health minister said flights involving Australia and the Netherlands would complete the evacuation Monday, and the MV Hondius was expected to depart for the Netherlands with about 30 crew members. The World Health Organization recommended a 42-day quarantine for passengers from the ship, while countries set different isolation rules for their nationals.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_8rSM5xV9cMKIhCkt41VbtTAIyoqfYValfODgCxUJ9ALwPZT0UN796255eFmTpIw7eKmaVI8SZ3HQpFXu6Iw5Hq9sAyx65WVwmJyWTRL04WJ' alt='People from the cruise ship MV Hondius, affected by a hantavirus outbreak, are transferred by boat to the port after disembarking, at the port of Granadilla de Abona, in Tenerife, Spain on May 10, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Evacuation process: Passengers moved from ship to shore in small groups under protective protocols, with medical tents, buses and flights arranged at Tenerife’s Granadilla port.</li><li>National protocols: Spain sent 14 nationals to Gómez Ulla Hospital in Madrid; France planned 72 hours of hospital monitoring followed by 45 days of home isolation for its evacuees.</li><li>UK arrangements: British evacuees were flown to Manchester, and reports said 22 UK citizens would enter hospital quarantine in Merseyside.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Department of Health and Human Services: HHS said the State Department airlift would not take every evacuee to the same place; officials would assess arrivals and route them for care and support based on condition. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/05/10/one-cruise-ship-passenger-returning-to-the-u-s-showing-mild-hantavirus-symptoms-00913723'>Politico</a>)</li><li>French Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu: Lecornu said the five evacuees would receive medical treatment, tests and check-ups after the in-flight concern. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3353069/french-evacuee-hantavirus-hit-ship-shows-symptoms-pm-says'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus: Tedros said the risk to the general public from the outbreak was low, while evacuation workers and passengers used protective gear. (<a href='https://www.independent.com.mt/articles/2026-05-10/world-news/Plane-carrying-Spanish-passengers-from-hantavirus-stricken-MV-Hondius-cruise-ship-leaves-for-Madrid-6736289586'>The Malta Independent</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/05/10/one-cruise-ship-passenger-returning-to-the-u-s-showing-mild-hantavirus-symptoms-00913723'>One American has tested positive for hantavirus, another has mild symptoms</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/05/11/rtbh-m11.html'>Reckless disembarkation of hantavirus-stricken MV Hondius exposes collapse of public health</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3353069/french-evacuee-hantavirus-hit-ship-shows-symptoms-pm-says'>French evacuee from hantavirus-hit ship shows ‘symptoms’, PM says</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/evacuation-of-passengers-from-virus-hit-cruise-ship-to-be-completed-on-monday'>Evacuation o